# Roles and permissions setup checklist (frontend)

> Generated by `auth:setup`. Do these steps, tick them, then delete this file. How roles and permissions work: https://github.com/Light-it-labs/lightit-auth-laravel/blob/main/docs/permission.md

- [ ] **Install dependencies** (`{{ packageManager }}`): {{ dependencyReport }}
- [ ] **Add the i18n keys** to `src/i18n/locales/en.json` and `es.json`: the `roles` block and
  `navigation.links.roles`. Copy them from **i18n keys to paste** below.
- [ ] **Link the roles page from the sidebar** in `src/routes/_private/-components/sidebar/sidebar.tsx`, only for
  users who can manage roles:
  1. Add `import { Can } from "@/components/permissions/can";` and
     `import { PERMISSIONS } from "@/services/permissions/constants";` with the other `@/` imports
  2. Add this right after `{links.map(...)}`, inside `<NavigationMenu.List>`:

```tsx
<Can permission={PERMISSIONS.manageRoles}>
  <SidebarLink
    icon={<Icons.Lock />}
    isExpanded={isExpanded}
    label={t("navigation.links.roles")}
    path="/roles"
  />
</Can>
```

Check it worked: run `vite` once (`dev` or `build`) so the router adds the `/roles` route, then
`{{ packageManager }} exec tsc --noEmit` passes, a super admin sees **Roles** in the sidebar and can change a user's
roles there, and a user without `roles.manage` doesn't see the link and is sent to `/` when opening `/roles`.

